+ ## What is DashPass?
+ Think of DashPass as a **safe deposit box that lives on a blockchain**.
+ - You have a **key** (called a WIF — a long string of characters). Only you have this key.
+ - Your secrets (API keys, passwords, tokens) go into the box, **locked with military-grade encryption** before they leave your computer.
+ - The locked box is stored on the **Dash network** — thousands of computers around the world keep a copy, so it's always available and can't be deleted by anyone.
+ - When you need a secret back, DashPass uses your key to unlock the box on your machine. The Dash network never sees the actual secret — it only stores the locked version.
+ **In plain English:** DashPass lets you store and retrieve passwords and API keys securely, using the Dash blockchain as tamper-proof storage. No company holds your data. No server to hack. Just you and your key.
