+ ## CLI Reference
+ All commands follow this pattern:
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs <command> [options]
+ 💡 All diagnostic messages go to **stderr**. The actual result goes to **stdout**. This means commands work correctly in scripts and pipes.
+ ### `put` — Store a new secret
+ Encrypts a value and saves it on Dash Platform.
+   --service <name> \
+   --type <type> \
+   --level <level> \
+   --value <value> \
+   [--label <label>]
+ | Flag | Required | Description |
+ |------|:--------:|-------------|
+ | `--service` | Yes | A unique name for this secret (max 63 characters). Use the pattern `provider-type`, e.g. `anthropic-api` |
+ | `--type` | Yes | What kind of secret (see table below) |
+ | `--level` | Yes | How sensitive: `normal`, `sensitive`, or `critical` |
+ | `--value` | Yes | The actual secret to encrypt and store |
+ | `--label` | No | A human-readable description (defaults to the service name) |
+ **Valid types:**
+ | Type | When to use | Examples |
+ |------|------------|---------|
+ | `api-key` | API keys for external services | Anthropic, OpenAI, Brave Search |
+ | `oauth-token` | OAuth/refresh tokens | GitHub, Google, Slack |
+ | `ssh-key` | SSH private keys | VPS access, Git deploy keys |
+ | `wif` | Blockchain private keys | Dash WIF keys |
+ | `db-cred` | Database passwords | PostgreSQL, Redis, MongoDB |
+ | `tls-cert` | TLS/SSL certificates | Server certs, client certs |
+ | `service-token` | Internal auth tokens | Webhook secrets, microservice tokens |
+ | `encryption-key` | Encryption passphrases | Backup encryption keys |
+ **Example — store an Anthropic API key:**
+   --service anthropic-api \
+   --service anthropic-api \
+   --level sensitive \
+   --value "sk-ant-api03-xxxxxxxxxxxx" \
+   --label "Anthropic production key"
+   Service:     anthropic-api
+   Level:       sensitive
+ ### `get` — Retrieve a secret
+ Fetches and decrypts a stored credential.
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs get --service <name> [--json] [--pipe]
+ | Flag | Description |
+ | Flag | Description |
+ |------|-------------|
+ |------|-------------|
+ | `--service` | The name you gave the secret when you stored it |
+ | `--json` | Show full details (metadata + value) instead of just the value |
+ | `--pipe` | Clean output for scripts — no logs, no trailing newline |
+ **Default mode — just the value:**
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs get --service anthropic-api
+ sk-ant-api03-xxxxxxxxxxxx
+ **JSON mode — value + metadata:**
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs get --service anthropic-api --json
+ ```json
+ {
+   "service": "anthropic-api",
+   "value": "sk-ant-api03-xxxxxxxxxxxx",
+   "type": "api-key",
+   "level": "sensitive",
+   "version": 1,
+   "status": "active",
+   "expiresAt": null,
+   "documentId": "ABcy3VXG3U5teNUTsXS7ZSkgJHeZgJaS7agx7UsyTrL5",
+   "source": "platform"
+ }
+ 💡 The `source` field tells you where the value came from: `"cache"` (fast, local copy) or `"platform"` (fetched from the network).
+ **Pipe mode — for use in scripts:**
+ # Store the value in a variable (no extra output, no trailing newline)
+ API_KEY=$(node dashpass-cli.mjs get --service anthropic-api --pipe 2>/dev/null)
+ echo "Key starts with: ${API_KEY:0:10}..."
+ ### `list` — See all your stored secrets
+ Shows a table of your credentials **without decrypting them** (only metadata is shown).
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs list [--type <type>] [--level <level>] [--status <status>]
+ | `--type` | Filter by type (e.g. `api-key`) |
+ | `--level` | Filter by level (`critical`, `sensitive`, `normal`) |
+ | `--status` | Filter by status (`active`, `archived`, `revoked`) |
+ **Example — list all active credentials:**
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs list --status active
+  Service              │ Type        │ Level     │ Ver │ Status │ Expires    │ Doc ID
+ ──────────────────────┼─────────────┼───────────┼─────┼────────┼────────────┼──────────────
+  anthropic-api        │ api-key     │ sensitive │ 1   │ active │ —          │ ABcy3VXG3U…
+  xai-api              │ api-key     │ sensitive │ 2   │ active │ —          │ GjTXtwrkAG…
+  github-oauth-ci      │ oauth-token │ sensitive │ 1   │ active │ 2026-07-01 │ 7kMnPqRs2x…
+ 3 credential(s) found.
+ 💡 `list` never shows actual secret values — it's safe to run in shared terminals.
+ ### `delete` — Revoke a secret
+ Marks a credential as revoked. The encrypted data stays on Platform but is no longer returned by `get` or `list --status active`.
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs delete --service <name>
+ **Example:**
+ **Example:**
+ **Example:**
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs delete --service old-webhook-secret
+ Revoking credential "old-webhook-secret" (doc ABcy3VXG...)...